21.docs:
Returns `true` if the queue is full.

An unbounded queue is never full.

# Examples

```
use concurrent_queue::ConcurrentQueue;

let q = ConcurrentQueue::bounded(1);

assert!(!q.is_full());
q.push(1).unwrap();
assert!(q.is_full());
```

